				<span>TypeScript &nbsp;·&nbsp; React &nbsp;·&nbsp; Effect TS &nbsp;·&nbsp; tRPC &nbsp;·&nbsp; Zod &nbsp;·&nbsp; Tailwind &nbsp;·&nbsp; AI-Native &nbsp;·&nbsp; Ship Fast &nbsp;·&nbsp; Type Safe &nbsp;·&nbsp; DX First &nbsp;·&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span>
			</div>
		</div>

		<!-- ABOUT -->
		<section class="container" style="padding-top: 80px; padding-bottom: 40px;">
			<div class="reveal card" style="background: var(--yellow); max-width: 960px; transform: rotate(-0.5deg);">
				<h2 style="font-size: 2rem; margin-bottom: 20px;">The Pitch</h2>
				<div style="font-size: 1.1rem; line-height: 1.7; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 16px;">
					<p><strong>Three years of production code. Two competing job offers. One obsession: making runtime errors impossible.</strong></p>
					<p>I started coding commercially at 19, building property management software with Spring Boot. Then Check24 — Germany's biggest comparison portal — where I scored their highest performance rating. Now I lead the frontend at Buildlinx, making architecture decisions for IoT building management.</p>
					<p>I live in the TypeScript ecosystem. Effect TS, tRPC, Zod, TanStack — the modern stack that most German companies haven't discovered yet. I follow Theo (t3.gg) and the San Francisco developer scene because that's where the future ships first.</p>
					<p>My AI workflow isn't experimental — it's essential. Cursor, Claude, and Codex are how I ship faster than teams twice my size.</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<!-- TECH STACK -->
		<section class="container" style="padding-top: 40px; padding-bottom: 40px;">
			<h2 class="reveal" style="font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3rem); margin-bottom: 32px; transform: rotate(1deg);">Sticker Collection 🧩</h2>

